
AppServe
--------

AppServe is a dynamically configurable application server for UNIX-like
systems.  It runs applications in multiple languages and exposes a control
API for configuration at runtime.

Listeners pass requests directly to applications and application targets.
Listener pass values can use request variables and NJS expressions.

AppServe continues the development and maintenance of NGINX Unit.

Source code and issue tracking:

  https://github.com/hongzhidao/AppServe

The repository is currently private; access is required to view the source,
report issues, and contribute changes.

Build from source:

  ./configure --prefix=/usr/local/appserve
  make
  make install

Run the daemon with appserved.  Use appserved --help for command-line options
and ./configure --help for build options.  Language modules are configured
separately, for example with ./configure python before running make.

See docs/migration.md for changes to executable names, packages, services,
and default paths when migrating from Unit.  Existing language binding and
libunit API names are retained for source compatibility.

See docs/release-notes.md for the 0.1.0 release and its verification status.

The upstream Unit documentation remains a reference for the inherited
configuration API and application support:

  https://unit.nginx.org

